.TH POWERSIFU 1 "23 September 2026" "PowerSifu 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
powersifu \- automate Linux desktop power profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B powersifu
.RI [ --background ]
.br
.B powersifu
.RI [ --foreground ]
.br
.B powersifu
.RI [ --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PowerSifu
is a GTK system-tray utility for power-profiles-daemon. It can select profiles
when AC power changes, apply profile-specific display brightness, run recurring
weekly schedules, install verified updates with system authentication, and gracefully terminate
configured same-user applications when a selected profile becomes active.
.PP
The settings window provides General, Brightness, Application Rules, Schedules, and About pages.
Closing the window leaves the tray process running. Use Quit in the tray menu to
stop PowerSifu.
.PP
By default, the command detaches the application from the calling terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --background
Start the tray service without opening the settings window.
.TP
.B --foreground
Keep the GTK process attached to the calling terminal for diagnostics.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed PowerSifu version and exit without starting the service.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/powersifu/config.json
Per-user configuration. The XDG_CONFIG_HOME environment variable is honored.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.tpluharik.PowerSifu.desktop
Per-user override for automatic login startup.
.SH SECURITY
Application rules accept exact executable names only. PowerSifu sends SIGTERM
to matching processes owned by the current user and protects core desktop
processes. It does not execute arbitrary commands or install privilege rules.
In-app updates verify package metadata before a fixed package-manager command
requests authorization through the operating system.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR powerprofilesctl (1),
.BR power-profiles-daemon (8)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/tpluharik/powersifu/issues.
